    <string name="onboarding_start">Set up</string>
    <string name="onboarding_finish">Done</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Before you set a PIN</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_subtitle">Three things worth knowing, because each one changes what you should store here.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_what">API keys, platform account passwords and access tokens are encrypted field by field with AES-256-GCM. Provider names, endpoints, model ids and balances are stored in the clear.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_limit">A six digit PIN does not stop someone who copies these files off the device and attacks them offline. So do not store a password here that you reuse elsewhere — the settings offer a long passphrase instead.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_recovery">The last step gives you a recovery key. It is the only way back in if you forget your PIN, so have somewhere to write it down.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_pin_title">Choose a 6 digit PIN</string>
    <string name="onboarding_pin_subtitle">The PIN only wraps the real data key, so changing it later re-wraps one small value and never re-encrypts your data.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_pin_confirm_title">Enter it again</string>
    <string name="onboarding_pin_confirm_subtitle">A typo here would lock you out on the very first unlock.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_pin_restart">Start over with a different PIN</string>
    <string name="onboarding_calibrating_title">Calibrating</string>
    <string name="onboarding_calibrating_subtitle">Measuring how long one key derivation takes on this device, so unlocking stays quick without weakening the settings.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_calibrating_note">This runs once, and cannot be cancelled. There is no progress to show: the derivation has no intermediate steps to report.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_biometric_title">Biometric unlock</string>
    <string name="onboarding_biometric_subtitle">Optional. You can turn it on or off later in Settings, Security.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_biometric_checking">Checking what this device supports…</string>
    <string name="onboarding_biometric_switch">Unlock with biometrics</string>
    <string name="onboarding_biometric_switch_summary">This is a second way to unwrap the same data key, not a second lock. The key sits in hardware and requires an authentication every time; adding or removing a fingerprint invalidates it and unlock falls back to the PIN.</string>
